course: dictionary
lesson: 6219
title: Misunderstand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To misunderstand something is to get its meaning wrong. The prefix mis- means wrongly, so misunderstand means understand wrongly. In maths you might misunderstand a question, so reading it twice helps you get the right meaning.
explain: Misunderstanding can also happen between people. «Things heard half through a door are often misunderstood and can be more frightening than the truth.» The listener fills the gaps with a wrong idea, and that idea can grow bigger than the real thing.
explain: In texts there is no voice or face to show what someone means. «Sarcasm is easily misunderstood» because the reader cannot hear the joking tone. Tone tags like /s and /j, or an emoji, give the reader clues about how the words should be taken.
fact: Misunderstand is a verb. Its other forms are misunderstands, misunderstood and misunderstanding.
fact: «Misunderstood» is also the past form, as in «I think you misunderstood».
fact: To misunderstand a person means to get the wrong idea about what they mean or what they are like.
fact: «Don't misunderstand me» is a useful phrase when you want to make your meaning clear.
fact: Talking calmly is a good way to put a misunderstanding right.
exercise: In maths you read a question twice so you do not misunderstand it. What does misunderstand mean? | To ask a question loudly | To understand something perfectly | *To get the meaning of something wrong | To forget a question
exercise: Ella says «I think you misunderstood» what she meant. Which word is the past form of misunderstand? | misunderstanding | *misunderstood | misunderstands | misunderstand it
exercise: «Children who never greet adults are often misunderstood as rude or upset, even when they are only shy.» What does misunderstood mean here? | Seen as very clever | Greeted warmly by everyone | *Wrongly thought to be rude or upset | Given a prize for good manners
test: Why can a text message be misunderstood? | Because phones cannot show words | Because messages are always too long | Because people never send messages | *Because there is no voice or face to show the tone
test: What helps stop sarcasm being misunderstood in a text? | Using a longer word | Sending the message late at night | Writing in capital letters only | *A tone tag like /j or an emoji
exam: Which sentence shows someone trying to stop a wrong idea about what they mean? | «She laughed at the funny joke.» | «The shop opens at nine.» | *«Don't misunderstand me, I meant it kindly.» | «We walked to the park after school.»
